# Typing on a RENDERED markdown preview swaps to the raw editor and the
# keystroke LANDS — it is not swallowed. User: "if user tries to type on
# md being previewed shoudl we go to edit mode or ask?" → go straight to
# edit; typing is unambiguous intent.

write notes.md "# Title\n\nSome text.\n"
open notes.md

# Opens rendered by default (`markdown_opens_rendered`), so the heading
# marker is stripped and the banner offers Edit.
expect screen lacks "# Title"
expect screen contains "Edit"

# Type one character.
type "Z"

# Raw source is on screen now — the `#` marker proves this is the editor
# and not the renderer, which strips it.
expect screen contains "# Title"

# ...and the character that triggered the swap actually landed.
expect dirty true
